        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0449111a-b5df-5c3a-b759-66ce19ef7b32",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Douglas\n- Songs: \"Man on the Edge\", \"Running Free\", \"Out of the Silent Planet\", \"Total Eclipse\", \"Mission From 'Arry\", \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\", \"I Live My Way\", \"Run to the Hills\", \"2 Minutes to Midnight\", \"Be Quick or Be Dead\"\n- Albums: Best of the 'B' Sides, The Number of the Beast\n- Films: Falling Down\n- Bands: Iron Maiden\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kirk Douglas was born on September 25, 1944, and he is an American actor and producer.\n- Iron Maiden's single \"Running Free\" was released in 1980.\n- Iron Maiden's single \"Total Eclipse\" was the B-side of \"Run to the Hills\" in 1982.\n- Iron Maiden's single \"Mission From 'Arry\" was the B-side of \"2 Minutes to Midnight\" in 1984.\n- Iron Maiden's single \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\" was the B-side of \"Be Quick or Be Dead\" in 1992.\n- Iron Maiden's song \"Man on the Edge\" is based on the film \"Falling Down\", which starred Michael Douglas.\n- Iron Maiden's single \"I Live My Way\" was the B-side of \"Man on the Edge\" in 1995.\n- From 1998 onward, \"Total Eclipse\" was added to Iron Maiden's album \"The Number of the Beast\".\n- Iron Maiden's compilation album Best of the 'B' Sides covers all of the band's singles from 1980's \"Running Free\" to 2000's \"Out of the Silent Planet\", except for several original B-sides that were excluded from the collection.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "17aa7cdb-09ce-5a14-891e-619ee3019501",
        "text": "Page: Man on the Edge. Sentence: The song is based on the film \"Falling Down\", starring Michael Douglas.\nPage: Michael Douglas. Sentence: Michael Kirk Douglas (born September 25, 1944) is an American actor and producer.\nPage: Best of the 'B' Sides. Sentence: It covers all of their singles from their first (1980's \"Running Free\") to 2000's \"Out of the Silent Planet\", although several of the band's original B-sides were excluded from the collection: \"Total Eclipse\" (from \"Run to the Hills\", 1982, although this has been added to the album \"The Number of the Beast\" from 1998 onwards), \"Mission From 'Arry\" (from \"2 Minutes to Midnight\", 1984); \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\" (from \"Be Quick or Be Dead\", 1992); and \"I Live My Way\" (from \"Man on the Edge\", 1995).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
